<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Assizes of Ariano</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1140</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Assizes of Ariano are a collection of laws issued by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roger-ii-of-sicily">Roger II of Sicily</a>, traditionally at an assembly in Ariano in 1140. Drawing on Roman and canon law, they set out the authority of the king over his new kingdom, protected the church and the weak, and punished treason, while allowing the different peoples of the realm to keep their own customs. They prepared the way for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitutions-of-melfi">Constitutions of Melfi</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/assizes-of-ariano.jpg" alt="Assizes of Ariano" width="320" height="306" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roger_II_Sicily.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
